                <pb facs="0915" n="801" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg801"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/441: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Lay</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-03-24T18:00:00-05:00">March 24, 1931—6
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>18. Your 52, March 23, 2 p.m. The Department would view with satisfaction any
                    arrangement acceptable to both Honduras and Nicaragua, but considers inadvisable
                    any attempt to influence the negotiations for the present at least until the
                    views of both parties are more concretely defined so that it would be possible
                    to work towards a solution agreeable to both.</p>
                <p>Please repeat to Managua.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Carr</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
